 34CL c  1980Ew02,1979Ca15: A 600-MeV proton beam was produced from the         
 34CL2c  synchrocyclotron at CERN-ISOLDE and bombarded a ScC{-2} target. The    
 34CL3c  {+45}Sc(p,8n3p) spallation reaction products diffused out of the target
 34CL4c  and reached a tungsten surface ionization source where potassium       
 34CL5c  isotopes were selectively ionized. The beam was extracted from the ion 
 34CL6c  source, separated by the ISOLDE analyzing magnet, and collected by a   
 34CL7c  mylar foil for |g-ray measurements and then a carbon foil for proton   
 34CL8c  measurements. |g rays were detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Time for  
 34CL9c  positron activities were determined using a 700-|mm thick silicon      
 34CLAc  detector. Protons were detected using a 20-|mm-700-|mm thick |DE-E     
 34CLBc  telescope of silicon surface barrier detectors with FWHM=50 keV.       
 34CLCc  Measured E|g(<5 MeV), I|g, E{-p}(>0.9 MeV), I{-p}. Deduced levels, J,  
 34CLDc  |p, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, parent {+35}K T{-1/2}, and      
 34CLEc  coefficients of the isobaric multiplet mass equation for A=35, T=3/2   
 34CLFc  quartets. Comparisons with shell-model calculations and the mirror     
 34CLGc  nucleus {+35}Cl. Also see abstracts 1978HaYH, 1979HaZY, 1979HaZT, and  
 34CLHc  1979AnZZ.                                                              
 34CL c  2018Sa54: A 36-MeV/nucleon {+36}Ar primary beam was produced from the  
 34CL2c  K500 cyclotron at Texas A&M University. The secondary {+35}K beam was  
 34CL3c  produced via the {+1}H({+36}Ar,{+35}K)2n reaction of {+36}Ar bombarding
 34CL4c  a LN{-2}-cooled hydrogen gas target, separated by MARS, and implanted  
 34CL5c  into a 45-|mm DSSD sandwiched between a 140-|mm SSSD and a 1-mm Si-pad 
 34CL6c  detector in a pulsed-beam mode. |e+|b{++}-delayed protons were detected
 34CL7c  by the implantation detector. |g rays were detected by two HPGe        
 34CL8c  detectors. Measured E{-p}(>300 keV), I{-p}, E|g, I|g, p|g-coin,        
 34CL9c  |g|g-coin. Deduced parent {+35}K T{-1/2}.                              
 34CL c  2019ChZU: Same beam production as 2018Sa54. {+35}K was implanted into  
 34CL2c  the AstroBox2 detector filled with 800-Torr P5 gas. |e+|b{++}-delayed  
 34CL3c  protons were detected by the implantation detector. |g rays were       
 34CL4c  detected by 4 Clover Ge detectors. Measured E{-p}(>100 keV), I{-p},    
 34CL5c  E|g, I|g, p|g-coin, |g|g-coin.                                         
 34CL c  Others: 1998Sc19, 2006Me04: {+35}K |b-NMR studies.                     
